From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:56:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] media: iris: only rescale decoder power when a bitstream
 buffer is queued

A capture QBUF with no bitstream buffer pending sets max_input_data_size
to 0, which drops the session from the bandwidth total. In a live stream
that happens every frame, so the DDR vote flaps between the floor and the
session's vote and each frame pays two interconnect commits on the QBUF
path.

Rescale on bitstream QBUF only, and drop the session from the totals when
its bitstream queue stops.

Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/tree/main/packages/kernel/patches (1036-media-iris-only-rescale-decoder-power-on-bitstream-queue.patch, fetched 7 Nov 2026)

[mzak: picked from armada-os 1036 for the OnePlus Pad 4 (SM8850, iris
 VPU4): our iris_vdec_qbuf() / iris_vb2_stop_streaming() are the same as
 the peer's base; applies unchanged. The armada-os patch carries no
 Signed-off-by of its author; carried with its authorship.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c  | 3 +++
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
index 1fae2da94..d4f2e1025 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
@@ -248,6 +248,9 @@ void iris_vb2_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
 	if (ret)
 		goto exit;
 
+	if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(q->type))
+		inst->max_input_data_size = 0;
+
 exit:
 	iris_helper_buffers_done(inst, q->type, VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
 	if (ret)
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
index f4f6d483f..8c79f469f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
@@ -467,9 +467,9 @@ int iris_vdec_qbuf(struct iris_inst *inst, struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *vbuf)
 						   MAXIMUM_FPS);
 			inst->frame_counter = 0;
 		}
-	}
 
-	iris_scale_power(inst);
+		iris_scale_power(inst);
+	}
 
 	return iris_queue_buffer(inst, buf);
 }
